From: relay12 contributors
Subject: [PATCH] d3d11on12: shim __nullterminated and drop a redundant extern

Two parse failures in src/main.cpp under GCC.

The PCOMPATVALUE typedef annotates its parameters with SAL1:
`__in __nullterminated const char *`. mingw-w64's sal.h defines __in and
__out_opt but not __nullterminated, and an unknown annotation inside a
parameter list cascades -- the reported 'stdcall' attribute, 'pValue' and
PCOMPATVALUE errors that follow are all downstream of it. This tree already
carries a shim for __in in pch.hpp; __nullterminated joins it there, defined
empty, since these annotations carry no codegen meaning.

`extern "C" extern BOOL WINAPI DllMain(...)` is accepted by MSVC and rejected
by GCC as an invalid use of extern in a linkage specification. The linkage
specification already provides external linkage, so the second extern is
redundant and goes.
---
diff --git a/include/pch.hpp b/include/pch.hpp
index ad266cf..d42039a 100644
--- a/include/pch.hpp
+++ b/include/pch.hpp
@@ -15,6 +15,10 @@
 #ifndef __in
 #define __in _In_
 #endif
+
+#ifndef __nullterminated
+#define __nullterminated
+#endif
 
 #ifdef WIN32_LEAN_AND_MEAN
 // This defines NTSTATUS and other types that are needed for kernel headers
diff --git a/src/main.cpp b/src/main.cpp
index 817e238..c4f397a 100644
--- a/src/main.cpp
+++ b/src/main.cpp
@@ -30,7 +30,7 @@ bool GetCompatValue(const char* str, UINT64* pValue)
 }
 
 //----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-extern "C" extern BOOL WINAPI DllMain(
+extern "C" BOOL WINAPI DllMain(
     HINSTANCE hInstance,
     UINT dwReason,
     LPVOID ) noexcept
